[b][size=5]Glossary[/size][/b]

Every term in the rule editor, in UI order. All checks are [b]snapshots[/b]: a condition says whether something is true [i]right now[/i] when the rule is evaluated, never "keep doing X until it changes".

[b][size=4]How a rule is evaluated[/size][/b]

[list]
[*]Every tick the [b]Global[/b] list is checked first, then the companion's own list, each [b]top to bottom[/b]. Priority is the list position; there is no separate priority number.
[*]A rule fires when its conditions pass, its target can be resolved and its action is possible right now. If any of those fail, the rule is skipped [i]for this tick[/i] and the next rule is tried.
[*]Each tick a companion may issue at most [b]one command per action slot[/b] (standard, move, swift, free). So a cast from a higher rule and a swift action from a lower rule can both fire in one tick; two rules that need the same slot: the upper one wins.
[*]While a standard-action command (cast, attack, item) is still running, lower rules wait; only rules [i]above[/i] it may pre-empt it.
[*][b]DoNothing[/b] is the one hard stop: everything below it is ignored while its conditions hold.
[*]In combat the lists are re-evaluated every ~3 s (configurable), out of combat every ~2 s — but out of combat only for rules carrying Combat → IsInCombat → No.
[*][b]Cooldown (rounds)[/b]: after the rule fires, it stays quiet for that many 6-second rounds. 0 = may fire every tick.
[*][b]Enabled[/b]: unticked rules are skipped entirely.
[/list]

[b][size=4]Condition subjects (who is checked)[/size][/b]

[list]
[*][b]Self[/b]: The companion this rule belongs to.
[*][b]Ally[/b]: [i]Any one[/i] party member or pet other than Self. Several Ally rows in the same group must all be true for the [b]same[/b] ally.
[*][b]AllyCount[/b]: Counts allies other than Self that satisfy the property; the count is compared with the number on the right (>= 1, < 3, …).
[*][b]Enemy[/b]: [i]Any one[/i] visible, living enemy currently in combat with the party. Several Enemy rows in a group must all be true for the [b]same[/b] enemy.
[*][b]EnemyCount[/b]: Counts those enemies; EnemyCount = 0 is a valid gate ("no enemy in combat").
[*][b]Enemy: biggest / lowest threat[/b]: Scans enemies in that order (threat ≈ attack bonus + expected damage per hit) and takes the first one that passes the row's property. Also decides which enemy [b]Condition target[/b] points at.
[*][b]Enemy: highest / lowest HP%, AC, Fort, Reflex, Will, HD[/b]: Same as above, sorted by that stat. Only the [i]first[/i] sorted subject in a group sets the order — a second one does not add a "must also be lowest X" test.
[*][b]Enemy: nearest[/b]: Same, sorted by distance to Self.
[*][b]Specific ally[/b]: One pinned companion or pet, picked by name.
[*][b]Combat[/b]: The fight as a whole: IsInCombat (Yes/No) and CombatRounds (6-second rounds since combat started).
[/list]

[b][size=4]Properties (what is checked)[/size][/b]

[list]
[*][b]HP%[/b] (number): Current HP as a percentage of max HP. Downed units count as 0.
[*][b]Current HP[/b] (number): Current hit points, flat; temporary HP not included.
[*][b]AC[/b] (number): Current Armor Class with every active buff and debuff.
[*][b]SaveFortitude / SaveReflex / SaveWill[/b] (number): Current saving-throw bonus.
[*][b]HitDice[/b] (number): Hit dice (character level without mythic ranks).
[*][b]HasBuff[/b] (buff): The unit carries exactly that buff (picked from the buff list). != means "is missing it".
[*][b]HasCondition[/b] (condition): The unit has that game condition (Paralyzed, Stunned, Frightened, Nauseated, Confused, Blinded, Prone, Entangled, Exhausted, Fatigued, Shaken, Sickened, Sleeping, Petrified, Slowed, Staggered, Dazed, Dazzled, Helpless, Cowering, Death's Door).
[*][b]Affected by[/b] (Poison / Disease / Bleed): Any active effect of that kind, no matter which spell or monster caused it.
[*][b]Immune to energy[/b] (Fire / Cold / Electricity / Acid / Sonic): The unit is fully immune to that energy type.
[*][b]CreatureType[/b] (type): Aberration, Animal, Construct, Dragon, Fey, Humanoid, Magical Beast, Monstrous Humanoid, Ooze, Outsider, Plant, Swarm, Undead, Vermin, Incorporeal. Uses the same type facts the game's own spells use; "Humanoid" means "none of the other types".
[*][b]Alignment[/b] (Good / Evil / Lawful / Chaotic / Neutral): Alignment axis. "Neutral" = neither Good nor Evil (LN, N, CN).
[*][b]HasClass[/b] (class or group): The unit has at least one level in that class, or belongs to the group: Spellcaster (has any spellbook), Arcane, Divine, Martial (a class that is neither arcane nor divine).
[*][b]IsDead[/b] (Yes/No): Truly dead — needs Raise Dead / Breath of Life. A companion who is down but will get up after the fight does [b]not[/b] count.
[*][b]Is summon[/b] (Yes/No): A summoned monster (Summon Monster, Animate Dead, …). Pets and companions are not summons.
[*][b]Is pet[/b] (Yes/No): Animal companion, Aivu, skeletal champion, eidolon, clone or similar.
[*][b]Wields ranged weapon[/b] (Yes/No): The unit's current weapon is a bow, crossbow, firearm, sling or thrown weapon. Re-checked every tick, so a weapon swap changes it.
[*][b]Is flanked[/b] (Yes/No): The game's own flanking state: at least two enemies are engaging the unit in melee (and it has no "cannot be flanked" feature). This is about attackers, not about being surrounded geometrically.
[*][b]Enemies adjacent[/b] (number): How many living enemies in combat stand within 2 m of the unit (centre to centre, so a large creature next to the unit can count as 0 — use [b]Enemies in melee (engaged)[/b] for "is this unit in melee").
[*][b]Enemies in melee (engaged)[/b] (number): How many living enemies the game itself treats as in melee with the unit: enemies it threatens plus enemies threatening it, each counted once. Uses the game's own reach (creature size + weapon reach, line of sight), so large creatures and reach weapons count. Self / Ally / AllyCount only.
[*][b]Ability damage[/b] (Yes/No): One of the six ability scores carries temporary damage (what Lesser Restoration cures). Drain is not counted.
[*][b]Negative levels[/b] (Yes/No): The unit has negative levels (energy drain), temporary or permanent.
[*][b]SpellSlotsAtLevel[/b] (spell level (+ optional count)): The unit still has at least one unused spell slot of exactly that level (any spellbook). Fill in the [i]Min. count[/i] field to compare the number of free slots with the operator instead, e.g. >= 2 keeps the last slot in reserve.
[*][b]SpellSlotsAboveLevel[/b] (spell level (+ optional count)): At least one unused slot of that level [i]or higher[/i]; with [i]Min. count[/i], the number of such slots is compared with the operator.
[*][b]Resource[/b] (resource): The unit has at least one use left of that class resource (Ki, Lay on Hands, Arcane Reservoir, …).
[*][b]WithinRange[/b] (bracket): Distance between Self and the checked unit — see Range brackets. Self → WithinRange is meaningless (always 0 m).
[*][b]DC − Save[/b] (number): Save DC of the spell this rule will cast minus the target's matching save — see DC − Save. Enemy subjects only.
[*][b]Hit margin (AB − AC)[/b] (number): An ally's attack bonus minus the enemy's AC — see Hit Margin. Enemy subjects only.
[*][b]HD − PartyMax[/b] (number): Enemy hit dice minus the party's highest character + mythic level. Positive = the enemy outlevels you. Enemy subjects only.
[*][b]Targeting me[/b] (Yes/No): This enemy's current attack or spell is aimed at Self. Enemy subjects only.
[*][b]Targeting ally[/b] (Yes/No): This enemy is aiming at a party member (optionally one pinned companion). Enemy subjects only.
[*][b]Targeted by ally[/b] (Yes/No): A party member (optionally a pinned one) is attacking this enemy. Enemy subjects only.
[*][b]Targeted by enemy[/b] (Yes/No): Some enemy is attacking this ally. Ally subjects only.
[*][b]IsInCombat[/b] (Yes/No): Whether the party is in combat. Subject Combat only — see Out-of-combat rules.
[*][b]CombatRounds[/b] (number): 6-second rounds elapsed since the current fight began. Subject Combat only.
[/list]

[b]Operators:[/b] <, >, <=, >=, =, !=. Yes/No properties only use = and !=. For [b]WithinRange[/b] the operator compares [i]brackets[/i], not meters: <= Short = within 10 m, < Short = within 5 m, = Short = the 5–10 m band only.

[b][size=4]Actions (what the companion does)[/size][/b]

[list]
[*][b]CastSpell[/b]: Casts the chosen spell. [i]Sources[/i] chooses where it may come from: spellbook (also wands in quickslots), scrolls, potions. Optional fallbacks are tried in order when the first spell is unavailable. Optional metamagic rod and Arcane Reservoir boost.
[*][b]CastAbility[/b]: Uses a class or racial ability that is not a spell (Lay on Hands, Kinetic Blast, Evil Eye, …).
[*][b]UseItem[/b]: Uses a specific usable item: an equipped wand/scroll/trinket first, otherwise from the shared inventory (potion, then scroll, then wand, then rods and other devices).
[*][b]ToggleActivatable[/b]: Switches a toggle ability (Power Attack, Fighting Defensively, stances, Smite …) [b]On[/b] or [b]Off[/b]. Fires only when the toggle is not already in that state.
[*][b]AttackTarget[/b]: Makes a normal weapon attack on the target.
[*][b]Heal[/b]: Picks a heal automatically. [i]Mode[/i] Strongest/Any = highest-ranked (spellbook spell by level > class feature > scroll > potion), Weakest = lowest-ranked. [i]Sources[/i] can exclude scrolls or potions. [i]Energy[/i] Auto heals living with Cure and undead with Inflict; Positive/Negative force one. Scrolls that would need a risky Use Magic Device check are only used as a last resort.
[*][b]ThrowSplash[/b]: Throws a splash weapon (Alchemist's Fire, Acid Flask, Holy Water …). Any = first in inventory, Strongest = highest damage, Cheapest = lowest value.
[*][b]Switch weapon set[/b]: Switches to weapon set 1–4.
[*][b]Move to target[/b]: Walks toward the target until within the chosen bracket ("stop within Melee / Cone / Short …"). Re-checked every tick, so a moving target is followed. Does nothing when already within that distance — which is why [b]Target: Self[/b] never moves. While the walk is running, lower rules that would need the move or standard action are held back.
[*][b]Move away from target[/b]: Walks away from the target until farther than the chosen bracket ("until beyond Short" = more than 10 m). Tries straight away first, then sideways and diagonal directions, and takes the reachable point that gains the most distance — a wall behind the unit yields a sideways escape; a cornered unit stays put. [b]Target: Self[/b] means "away from the enemies around me" (those within 10 m, else the nearest). Re-checked every tick, so a pursuing enemy triggers the next step, and lower move/standard rules are held while the walk runs, same as Move to target. Pair it with a condition such as Self → Is flanked → Yes or Self → Enemies adjacent → >= 2.
[*][b]DoNothing[/b]: Issues no command and stops every rule below it for this tick. Use it as a blocker, e.g. "if Self HP% < 20 do nothing" above a charge rule.
[/list]

[b][size=4]Targets (whom the action is aimed at)[/size][/b]

[list]
[*][b]Self[/b]: The companion itself.
[*][b]Ally: lowest HP[/b]: Party member or pet (not Self) with the lowest HP%.
[*][b]Ally with condition[/b]: First ally (not Self) with the chosen condition.
[*][b]Ally missing buff[/b]: First ally (not Self) without the chosen buff.
[*][b]Specific ally[/b]: One pinned companion or pet.
[*][b]Ally: most clustered (5 m)[/b]: The ally with the most other living allies within 5 m — for area buffs.
[*][b]Enemy: nearest / lowest HP / highest HP / highest AC / lowest AC / … / highest HD / lowest HD[/b]: Sorts the visible enemies in combat by that stat and takes the first.
[*][b]Enemy: highest threat[/b]: Enemy with the highest threat score (attack bonus + expected damage). Default target for attack rules.
[*][b]Enemy: creature type[/b]: First enemy of the chosen creature type.
[*][b]Enemy: most clustered (5 m)[/b]: The enemy with the most other enemies within 5 m — for Fireball-style spells.
[*][b]Condition target[/b]: The unit that made the conditions pass: the enemy matched by an Enemy row, else the ally matched by an Ally row, else Self when only Self rows matched.
[*][b]Condition target (ally)[/b]: The ally matched by an Ally row, even when an Enemy row in the same group also matched. Never the companion itself. Without a matched ally the rule is skipped, also for Heal and Toggle.
[*][b]Point at self[/b]: A ground point ~1.5 m in front of the companion — for summons and ground-targeted spells.
[*][b]Point at condition target[/b]: A ground point ~1.5 m from the condition target, on the side facing the companion. Same enemy > ally > self preference as [b]Condition target[/b].
[/list]

If the target cannot be resolved (no enemy of that type, no ally missing the buff, …), the rule is skipped for this tick and the next rule is tried.
